v 3
d alluvial (fork of Asjad Naqvi's alluvial): adds label, ordering and flow-merging options.
d
d valdec1        - whole number if the value is >=1, one decimal if <1 (flow values and category %).
d valnudge(#)    - de-collide value labels where thin flows converge on a narrow node (0 = off).
d sortsize(...)  - order nodes within a column by size (largest at top) instead of alphabetically.
d mergeflows(#)  - merge the ribbons arriving at a column into one river before they split.
d flowsort(...)  - set the ribbon stacking order (wires up an upstream hook that was never settable).
d valdec(#)      - fixed number of decimals for flow values and category %.
d pctbase        - with percent2, category % as a share of the first column instead of each column.
d stagen         - funnel view: columns as % of those reaching them, flows labelled with counts.
d
d All additions are opt-in: omit them and output is byte-identical to the upstream behaviour.
d
d Requires: palettes, colrspace, graphfunctions (from SSC).
d
d Original: https://github.com/asjadnaqvi/stata-alluvial
d
f alluvial.ado
f alluvial.sthlp
